title ALES155 — Lotus's stereo_dc_remove: the DC-offset remover carried into stereo, two independent means, the image-preserving translation opposite the rectifier's collapse
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Second rung this turn (after ALES154 stereo_smooth_trim, sent). The silence/analysis family is now whole in stereo (146-154), so I turned to the still-unlifted processing rungs. dc_remove (ALES90) and dc_block (ALES91) are the highest mono rungs with no stereo twin, and DC removal is the tool every chain reaches for right after a nonlinearity — the crux that lets the even-harmonic drive family be used honestly in stereo. Ascending order takes the block-mean remover (90) first, the foundation of the one-pole blocker (91).
think This is a LENGTH-PRESERVING per-channel lift, so it takes ALES138 stereo_rectify's shape (validate span once against shared length, run mono on each channel), NOT the silence family's lockstep. The stereo insight: the two channels carry their OWN offsets, so each removes its OWN mean independently — no desync wall because no length changes. The nice counterpoint: where the rectifier is an EVEN map that COLLAPSES an out-of-phase master to mono, DC removal is a per-channel PURE TRANSLATION that PRESERVES every sample-to-sample difference, so it PRESERVES the image — an out-of-phase master riding a common offset returns still out of phase. Two poles of the same stereo field, ALES155 answering ALES138.
think StereoDcError = ALES90's DcError (BadRange) reused whole. Five laws witnessed: stereo DC-remove law (=ALES90 mono byte for byte, left +1100 / right -500), independent-offset law (big left + small right offsets each under one LSB independently, zero-mean channel unchanged while partner corrected), image-preserve law (out-of-phase master riding common +1000 returns still exactly out of phase, both-zero-mean unchanged, idempotent), composition law (undoes stereo_rectify's per-channel offset: rectified left 18000 / right 12000 each removed to near-zero), balance/atomicity/degenerate. First-try witness GREEN.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, values only through the proven mono remover (two-pass block statistic per channel, sum in i64, memoryless), a self-approved design round. First-try GREEN, no red. Recorded lesson: a length-preserving per-channel value map lifts by the ANALYSIS/effect corner (validate once on the shared length, run mono per channel, no lockstep), and the stereo-specific law is about what the map does to the IMAGE — an EVEN map (rectify) collapses antisymmetry, a TRANSLATION (dc_remove) preserves it. Naming the image behaviour is the stereo crux for every value map, distinct from the silence family whose crux is the joint-silence lockstep. Witness GREEN (stereo law, independent-offset, image-preserve, composition undoing ALES138, balance/atomicity/degenerate), TAME bans clean, width exit 0. Front doors lotus/README.md and session-logs/README.md synced.
loom witness=ales_stereo_dc_remove_witness result=GREEN laws=stereo-dc-remove-law+independent-offset+image-preserve channels=2 class=stereo-effect-length-preserving lift=per-channel-value-map(ALES138-shape) form=validate-once-run-mono-per-channel image=translation-PRESERVES(opposite-rectify-collapse) cases=stereo-law(=ALES90-mono,left+1100/right-500)+independent-offset(big-left+small-right-each-under-LSB,zero-mean-channel-unchanged)+image-preserve(out-of-phase+common-1000-stays-out-of-phase,both-zero-mean-unchanged,idempotent)+composition(undoes-ALES138:rect-18000/12000-removed)+balance/atomicity(BadRange-untouched-balanced,count0-empty-identity) reds=0
